---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="One sick service, one home screen" hint="The home screen needs five services. Pick how the BFF calls them and which service is sick, then watch 2,000 simulated screen opens.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with <b>parallel, wait for all</b> and a sick <b>recommendations</b> service that hangs on 20% of calls: the typical screen is fast, but <b>1 open in 5 hangs for 8,000 ms</b>, so the 95th percentile is 8,000 ms, because the BFF waits for a part that is only a nice-to-have.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>per-call timeouts</b>: the 95th percentile drops to <b>100 ms</b> and the missing part makes the screen partial. But about <b>4% of screens now fail</b> even with nothing sick, because a rare slow call (250 ms) on a required part now counts as an error.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>Timeouts, retry required, stale for optional</b>: failures go to <b>0%</b> and the screen stays at <b>100 ms</b> at the 95th percentile. Now make <b>orders</b> the sick service: required parts cannot be faked, so about <b>4% still fail</b> (a hang twice in a row), which is honest.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg mbb" data-mbb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>How the BFF calls them <select class="pg-in" data-mode>
        <option value="seq">One after another, no timeouts</option>
        <option value="wait" selected>Parallel, wait for all</option>
        <option value="tmo">Parallel, per-call timeouts</option>
        <option value="full">Timeouts, retry required, stale for optional</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Sick service <select class="pg-in" data-sick>
        <option value="-1">None</option>
        <option value="2" selected>Recommendations (optional)</option>
        <option value="1">Orders (required)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Calls that hang (%) <input type="range" min="0" max="50" value="20" data-pct /> <b data-pctval></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Time to show the screen</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Complete screens</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Partial or stale screens</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Failed screens</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bar" role="img" data-bar aria-label="Share of complete, partial and failed screens"><span class="s1" data-s1></span><span class="s2" data-s2></span><span class="s3" data-s3></span></div>
    <p class="pg-note">Green is complete, amber is partial or stale, red is failed.</p>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: profile, orders, recommendations, promotions and inbox are called for each open. Normal latencies are 15 to 90 ms, and 2% of calls are slow by 250 ms. A hung call never answers until the client gives up at 8,000 ms. Timeouts are 120, 150, 100, 80 and 80 ms. A retry is one more call after the first timeout. 90% of opens have a stale copy of an optional part in the cache. Profile and orders are required, the rest are optional.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style>
  .bar { display: flex; height: 14px; border-radius: 7px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--surface-2); margin: 12px 0 4px; }
  .bar span { display: block; height: 100%; }
  .bar .s1 { background: var(--good); }
  .bar .s2 { background: var(--role-4); }
  .bar .s3 { background: var(--bad); }
</style>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-mbb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const SERVICES = [
      { name: 'profile', required: true, timeout: 120, base: 30, spread: 40 },
      { name: 'orders', required: true, timeout: 150, base: 40, spread: 60 },
      { name: 'recs', required: false, timeout: 100, base: 30, spread: 60 },
      { name: 'promos', required: false, timeout: 80, base: 20, spread: 50 },
      { name: 'inbox', required: false, timeout: 80, base: 15, spread: 30 },
    ];
    const N = 2000; const HANG = 8000; const TAIL = 250;
    const SEED = 2026; const TAIL_SHARE = 0.02; // 2% of calls pay the TAIL latency
    const STALE_HIT = 0.9; // share of optional parts with a stale copy to fall back on
    const P95 = 0.95; const P99 = 0.99; const SLOW_P95_MS = 1000;
    let seed = SEED; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    // All random draws are made once, so changing a control changes only the policy, never the luck.
    const draws = Array.from({ length: N }, () => SERVICES.map(() => ({ a: rnd(), t: rnd(), h: rnd(), a2: rnd(), h2: rnd(), s: rnd() })));
    function simulate(mode: string, sick: number, hangPct: number) {
      const times: number[] = []; let fresh = 0; let degraded = 0; let failed = 0;
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        const wait: number[] = []; const missing: boolean[] = []; let stale = 0;
        SERVICES.forEach((s, j) => {
          const d = draws[i][j];
          let lat = s.base + Math.floor(d.a * s.spread) + (d.t < TAIL_SHARE ? TAIL : 0);
          if (j === sick && d.h * 100 < hangPct) lat = HANG;
          let w = lat; let miss = false;
          if (mode === 'tmo' || mode === 'full') { w = Math.min(lat, s.timeout); miss = lat > s.timeout; } else miss = lat >= HANG;
          if (miss && mode === 'full' && s.required) {
            const lat2 = s.base + Math.floor(d.a2 * s.spread);
            const hung2 = j === sick && d.h2 * 100 < hangPct;
            w = s.timeout + Math.min(hung2 ? HANG : lat2, s.timeout); miss = hung2 || lat2 > s.timeout;
          }
          wait.push(w); missing.push(miss);
          if (miss && mode === 'full' && !s.required && d.s < STALE_HIT) { missing[j] = false; stale++; }
        });
        times.push(mode === 'seq' ? wait.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) : Math.max(...wait));
        const reqMiss = SERVICES.some((s, j) => s.required && missing[j]);
        if (reqMiss) failed++; else if (missing.some(Boolean) || stale > 0) degraded++; else fresh++;
      }
      times.sort((a, b) => a - b);
      const pc = (p: number) => times[Math.floor(N * p)];
      return { p50: pc(0.5), p95: pc(P95), p99: pc(P99), fresh, degraded, failed };
    }
    const fmt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const pct = (n: number) => `${((n / N) * 100).toFixed(1)}%`;
    const names = ['profile', 'orders', 'recommendations', 'promotions', 'inbox'];
    function draw() {
      const mode = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mode]').value; const sick = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-sick]').value); const hp = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-pct]').value);
      q('[data-pctval]').textContent = `${hp}%`;
      const r = simulate(mode, sick, hp);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `p50 ${fmt(r.p50)} ms, p95 ${fmt(r.p95)} ms`; q('[data-n1]').textContent = `p99 ${fmt(r.p99)} ms`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = pct(r.fresh); q('[data-n2]').textContent = `${fmt(r.fresh)} of ${fmt(N)} opens`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = pct(r.degraded); q('[data-n3]').textContent = `${fmt(r.degraded)} opens with a part missing or old`;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = pct(r.failed); q('[data-n4]').textContent = `${fmt(r.failed)} opens with a required part missing`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', r.p95 > SLOW_P95_MS ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--role-4)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', r.failed > 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--border)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-s1]').style.width = `${(r.fresh / N) * 100}%`; q<HTMLElement>('[data-s2]').style.width = `${(r.degraded / N) * 100}%`; q<HTMLElement>('[data-s3]').style.width = `${(r.failed / N) * 100}%`;
      q('[data-bar]').setAttribute('aria-label', `Complete ${pct(r.fresh)}, partial or stale ${pct(r.degraded)}, failed ${pct(r.failed)}`);
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const bad = r.p95 > SLOW_P95_MS || r.failed > 0; out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      const who = sick >= 0 ? names[sick] : 'nothing';
      let t: string;
      if (r.p95 > SLOW_P95_MS) t = `Too slow: 1 open in 20 takes ${fmt(r.p95)} ms or more. With no per-call timeout, a hung ${who} call holds the whole screen until the client gives up at ${fmt(HANG)} ms.`;
      else if (r.failed > 0 && (mode === 'tmo')) t = `Fast, but ${pct(r.failed)} of screens fail. A timeout turns a rare slow call to a required part into an error${sick === 1 ? ', and the hanging orders service adds many more' : ''}. A retry helps with slow calls, but not with a service that stays down.`;
      else if (r.failed > 0) t = `Fast, but ${pct(r.failed)} of screens fail. A required part cannot be skipped, and it hung on the first call and again on the retry.`;
      else if (mode === 'full') t = `Fast and never failing: required parts get a second try, and optional parts come from a stale copy when they time out. The price is that some screens show old data.`;
      else if (mode === 'seq') t = `Nothing fails, but calling the services one after another adds their times together: the median screen takes ${fmt(r.p50)} ms where a parallel fan-out with timeouts takes ${fmt(simulate('tmo', sick, hp).p50)} ms.`;
      else t = `Everything is fast and nothing fails, because nothing is sick enough to matter in this setting.`;
      out.textContent = t;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
